+# Phase-one scope audit
+
+**Date:** 2026-08-30
+
+This note resolves the owner's instruction to finish “phase one” against the
+two authoritative project documents. The terms **Phase A** and **PHASE 1** name
+different things and must not be used interchangeably.
+
+## Scheduled Phase A is already complete
+
+The day-by-day schedule defines **Phase A as Weeks 1–5: infrastructure, gate,
+and calibration**. It ends with the signed Gate 1 record at the end of Week 5.
+Weeks 1–3 and Weeks 4–5 have been completed; external Sol certified Weeks 4–5
+under D-120. The project has therefore already finished its first scheduled
+phase.
+
+Gate 1's final outcome is **FAIL**, and that is a completed adjudication rather
+than missing work:
+
+- reliability: PASS at rung 0;
+- compute: NOT ADJUDICABLE across the historical and current hosts;
+- permutation calibration: PASS;
+- five-percentage-point MDE condition: FAIL;
+- overall Gate 1: FAIL.
+
+The project continued with the registered 300-unit design and its disclosed
+power limitation. Turning the completed FAIL into a PASS by changing the
+sample, gate, host arithmetic, or criterion would be a new scientific decision,
+not completion of Phase A.
+
+The current scheduled position is therefore **Phase B, Week 6 closeout**.
+Week-6 machine work is complete, but local closure still requires the student's
+independent approximately 400-word explanation; external certification of
+D-141–D-152 remains pending.
+
+## Project-plan PHASE 1 is a repeated pipeline stage
+
+The project plan separately labels the following per-condition, per-seed loop
+as **PHASE 1 — data generation**:
+
+1. use the authorised exploratory policy;
+2. collect the configured transition dataset;
+3. train the registered world-model ensemble;
+4. evaluate on held-out transitions; and
+5. record failure traces above the frozen threshold.
+
+This loop is repeated inside later experiments; it has no standalone calendar
+gate and is not a project phase that can be globally closed now. It is complete
+for the 150/150 Experiment-1 baseline fits recorded by D-150. It is not complete
+for Experiment 2A, Experiment 2B, the configuration sweep, or later families,
+because those are scheduled Phase-B-and-later experiments with unresolved
+interfaces and rulings.
+
+## Autonomous boundary reached
+
+No further unattended scientific execution is safe merely from the phrase
+“finish phase one.” The following remain explicit stops:
+
+- the student-authored Week-6 explanation cannot be ghost-written;
+- external Sol must review D-141–D-152, the raw-tail inspection, and the strict
+  `>20%` conformance correction;
+- missing model-repair assignments (seven canonical and 173 whole-design)
+  cannot be guessed;
+- the Week-7/Week-10 confirmatory-look timing needs a ruling;
+- Experiment-1 production label/figure/trend adapters require a specification
+  and synthetic tests before any result payload is opened;
+- Experiment 2A, sweep, reserve, real critic split, threshold changes, and
+  design expansion remain stopped.
+
+This audit read schedule/plan/source/state only. It opened no confirmatory
+payload, computed no scientific statistic, launched no fit, used no GPU, and
+changed no existing evidence artifact.
